PART B — LUMINA OPEN UI LICENSE 1.0
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

In plain English: use it in anything you build, for free, forever. Just don't
repackage the kit itself and sell or give it away as a competing kit.

1. Grant. LuminaBench grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive,
   perpetual license to use, copy, modify and combine the materials covered by
   Part B (the "Materials") inside your own end products: websites, web and
   mobile apps, SaaS products, internal tools, games, client projects,
   prototypes and documentation, whether personal or commercial.

2. No attribution required. You do not need to credit LuminaBench in your end
   products or their source code.

3. Shipping is fine. Your end products may include the Materials in source or
   compiled form, and you may share their source code (including in public or
   open-source repositories), as long as the Materials are part of a product
   that does something beyond offering the Materials themselves.

4. Restrictions. You may not, in whole or substantial part, alone or bundled:
   (a) redistribute, sell, sublicense or rent the Materials as a UI kit,
       component library, design system, theme, template pack, palette pack,
       chart library, icon or token set, dataset or Agent Skill;
   (b) rebrand the Materials and offer them as your own kit or skill;
   (c) use the Materials, the catalog or its aliases as a training or
       evaluation dataset for a product that competes with this kit.
   Forking this repository on GitHub to contribute changes back, or to keep a
   private copy for your own projects, is permitted.

5. Ownership. LuminaBench keeps all rights not expressly granted. Your own
   modifications and your end products remain yours.

6. Termination. This license ends automatically if you break section 4. It is
   restored if you stop within 30 days of notice.

7. No warranty. The Materials are provided "as is", without warranty of any
   kind. LuminaBench is not liable for any claim or damages arising from their
   use.

Questions about what counts as a competing kit: https://luminabench.com
